//! ORIGIN NOTICE: this file is a conversion, made with the assistance of a language model and checked by a person, of
//! logic that already existed in the earlier tools Zartex and Zartex 2 (the Zartex 2 Lua mission script class and its compiler).
//! The logic is not original to this repository. What this repository adjusted, added or corrected in it:
//! - generated by tools_gen_api.py from the C# LuaMissionScript source, then reviewed
//!
//! Lua bindings for the mission logic node creators. Each `pub fn` builds one logic node in the script state, and
//! `register_generated` makes these functions callable from a Lua mission script under their Lua names.
//!
//! This file is generated by tools_gen_api.py, which reads oracle\api_methods.json (built from LuaMissionScript.cs by
//! tools_extract_api.py and tools_methods.py) and writes this file, api_consts.rs and nodenames.rs. The generator
//! lists what it could not translate in tools\gen_report.txt; those parts are written by hand in the api_* files.
//! The comment lines in this file were added after generation and are lost when the generator runs again.
//!
//! Exposes: `register_generated` (called with `dpl` false by compile.rs and with `dpl` true by api_dpl.rs) and the
//! `pub fn` node creators. Uses: binio, logic (PropValue), luaapi (Args, ret_node, rt_err) and script (ScriptState,
//! node_color). Used by: compile.rs, api_dpl.rs and api_part_c.rs (actor_creation, countdown_intro).
//!
//! Pattern of a node creator (the same for every function, so it is described once here):
//! - Actor arguments are `Option<usize>`, an index into the mission's actor definitions. Where the index is needed,
//!   `None` gives an error through `nre`.
//! - Where an actor must have a given kind, the function reads `type_id` of that actor and returns an error with
//!   the argument number. The ids are the ACTOR_NODE_TYPES ids in nodenames.rs (for example 3 for a Vehicle).
//! - The colour is built from the r, g and b arguments by `node_color`.
//! - `create_node` is called with the logic node type id (the id of the node name in nodenames.rs), the note, the
//!   colour and a closure that returns the list of properties. Each property is added with `prop(name, type_id, value)`;
//!   the type_id there is the property type (for example 7 for an actor reference, 20 for a localised text id and 9
//!   for flags), taken from the PROP table of tools_gen_api.py.
//! - Some functions do not build a node themselves but call another creator with fixed values (for example
//!   `has_clock_runned_out` calls `overlay_clock_watch`).
//!
//! Pattern of a registration block (one per Lua function in `register_generated`):
//! - `Args::new` gets the Lua arguments. Each `a.int`, `a.float`, `a.byte`, `a.boolean`, `a.string` or `a.actor` call
//!   reads one argument by position. A default value (`Some(...)`) is used when the argument is missing; `None`
//!   makes the argument required.
//! - The creator is called with `st2.borrow_mut()`, and `ret_node` turns the returned node and wire indexes into the
//!   Lua return value.
